{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-26958",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "filippo.io/edwards25519: filippo.io/edwards25519: Cryptographic integrity bypass due to incorrect MultiScalarMult results"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "filippo.io/edwards25519 is a Go library implementing the edwards25519 elliptic curve with APIs for building cryptographic primitives. In versions 1.1.0 and earlier, MultiScalarMult produces invalid results or undefined behavior if the receiver is not the identity point. If (*Point).MultiScalarMult is called on an initialized point that is not the identity point, it returns an incorrect result. If the method is called on an uninitialized point, the behavior is undefined. In particular, if the receiver is the zero value, MultiScalarMult returns an invalid point that compares Equal to every other point. Note that MultiScalarMult is a rarely used, advanced API. For example, users who depend on filippo.io/edwards25519 only through github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql are not affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-26958",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-26958\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: filippo.io/edwards25519\nFixed Version: 1.1.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-26958](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-26958)\nfilippo.io/edwards25519 is a Go library implementing the edwards25519 elliptic curve with APIs for building cryptographic primitives. In versions 1.1.0 and earlier, MultiScalarMult produces invalid results or undefined behavior if the receiver is not the identity point. If (*Point).MultiScalarMult is called on an initialized point that is not the identity point, it returns an incorrect result. If the method is called on an uninitialized point, the behavior is undefined. In particular, if the receiver is the zero value, MultiScalarMult returns an invalid point that compares Equal to every other point. Note that MultiScalarMult is a rarely used, advanced API. For example, users who depend on filippo.io/edwards25519 only through github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql are not affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.1.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-26958**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|filippo.io/edwards25519|1.1.1|[CVE-2026-26958](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-26958)|\n\nfilippo.io/edwards25519 is a Go library implementing the edwards25519 elliptic curve with APIs for building cryptographic primitives. In versions 1.1.0 and earlier, MultiScalarMult produces invalid results or undefined behavior if the receiver is not the identity point. If (*Point).MultiScalarMult is called on an initialized point that is not the identity point, it returns an incorrect result. If the method is called on an uninitialized point, the behavior is undefined. In particular, if the receiver is the zero value, MultiScalarMult returns an invalid point that compares Equal to every other point. Note that MultiScalarMult is a rarely used, advanced API. For example, users who depend on filippo.io/edwards25519 only through github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql are not affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.1.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 1.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39828",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: Unauthorized command execution via discarded SSH permissions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39828",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39828\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: 0.52.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-39828](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39828)\nWhen an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39828**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|golang.org/x/crypto|0.52.0|[CVE-2026-39828](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39828)|\n\nWhen an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39835",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: golang: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: Denial of Service via crafted SSH certificate"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SSH servers which use CertChecker as a public key callback without setting IsUserAuthority or IsHostAuthority could be caused to panic by a client presenting a certificate. CertChecker now returns an error instead of panicking when these callbacks are nil."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39835",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39835\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: 0.52.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-39835](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39835)\nSSH servers which use CertChecker as a public key callback without setting IsUserAuthority or IsHostAuthority could be caused to panic by a client presenting a certificate. CertChecker now returns an error instead of panicking when these callbacks are nil.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39835**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|golang.org/x/crypto|0.52.0|[CVE-2026-39835](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39835)|\n\nSSH servers which use CertChecker as a public key callback without setting IsUserAuthority or IsHostAuthority could be caused to panic by a client presenting a certificate. CertChecker now returns an error instead of panicking when these callbacks are nil."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
